<title>JAPAN: Japan Dec crude imports up 0.6 pct yr/yr - MITI.</title>
<headline>Japan Dec crude imports up 0.6 pct yr/yr - MITI.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Ministry of International Trade and Industry (MITI) on Tuesday issued the following data on crude oil imports during December 1996:</p>
<p> CRUDE OIL   (1,000 kl) (1,000 bbl) mth/mth% yr/yr%</p>
<p> Iran	   2,264	 14,241    -26.6    +52.0</p>
<p> Saudi Arabia 5,683	 35,746    +25.3    +18.4</p>
<p> Kuwait	 1,152	  7,246    - 9.0    - 6.4</p>
<p> Neutral Zone   967	  6,082    -13.0    -33.6</p>
<p> Qatar	  1,150	  7,234    +48.4    -10.4</p>
<p> Oman	   1,505	  9,466    +36.3    -11.0</p>
<p> UAE	    6,072	 38,193    - 7.5    - 4.3</p>
<p> Yemen	  -----	 ------    -----    -----</p>
<p> China	  1,150	  7,234    +21.9    +30.2</p>
<p> Malaysia	 474	  2,981    +38.2    -15.6</p>
<p> Brunei	   233	  1,466    -11.4    -33.8</p>
<p> Indonesia    1,524	  9,586    +42.6    - 6.4</p>
<p> Vietnam	  254	  2,233    -50.1    -52.7</p>
<p> Mexico	   411	  1,598    -27.5   +216.5</p>
<p> Australia	276	  1,736    - 8.6    -18.9</p>
<p> TOTAL	 23,117	145,406    + 2.8    + 0.6</p>
</text>
